From bf678c9ddf49afce3308dedbcefd793704c0d586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:01:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D6: cache app.js and app.css for good when the URL names
 their hash

Every page already linked /assets/app.css and /assets/app.js with a short
content hash (?v=), computed once at startup in layout.ts, but the server
answered every request with the same hour-long cache. A request carrying
the current hash is for exactly the content being served, so it now gets
"public, max-age=31536000, immutable"; the next deploy that changes either
file changes its URL. A request without the hash, or with a stale one,
keeps max-age=3600, so it is never pinned to content it did not name.
There is no service worker, and neither the manifest nor tools/shoot.mjs
references the two files, so nothing else needed the version.

Tests: asset-version.test.ts checks the hash matches the content, that
pages (including the 404 page) link both files by it, and the two cache
policies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016zXWwzys3K4XksLh3rrcKu
